<title>CANADA: Canadian grain body estimates barley quality.</title>
<headline>Canadian grain body estimates barley quality.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian Grain Commission on Monday released preliminary estimates of barley quality.</p>
<p>PROVINCE  Number of  Protein Content (PCT)</p>
<p>	    Samples    Mean Avg  Min. Max.</p>
<p>		 Extra 1 Canada Western</p>
<p>Man.	   85	11.8     10.0  13.6</p>
<p>Sask.	 196	11.3	8.6  14.5</p>
<p>Alta.	 167	11.9	8.3  16.1</p>
<p>Prairies    448	11.6	8.3  16.1</p>
<p>		 No1 CW</p>
<p>Man.	   25	11.9	9.8  14.4</p>
<p>Sask.	  30	11.7	9.6  14.5</p>
<p>Alta.	  36	11.8	9.5  16.0</p>
<p>Prairies     91	11.8	9.5  16.0</p>
<p>		 No2 CW</p>
<p>Man.	    3	12.0     10.7  14.1</p>
<p>Sask.	   8	11.7     10.8  12.8</p>
<p>Alta.	  11	12.6     11.1  15.2</p>
<p>Prairies     22	12.2     10.7  15.2</p>
<p>		 ALL GRADES</p>
<p>Man.	  113	11.8	9.8  14.4</p>
<p>Sask.	 234	11.3	8.6  14.5</p>
<p>Alta.	 214	11.9	8.3  16.1</p>
<p>Prairies    561	11.7	8.3  16.1</p>
<p>N.B.: final quality estimates may be issued at the end of November or in early December, CGC spokesman Paul Graham said.</p>
<p>-- Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548</p>
</text>
